            <ArticleTitle>A practical molecular identification of nonfermenting Gram-negative bacteria from cystic fibrosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1517-8382(17)30169-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bjm.2017.07.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Identification of nonfermenting Gram-negative bacteria (NFGNB) of cystic fibrosis patients is hard and misidentification could affect clinical outcome. This study aimed to propose a scheme using polymerase chain reaction to identify NFGNB. This scheme leads to reliable identification within 3 days in an economically viable manner when compared to other methods.</AbstractText>
